{
  "schemaVersion": 2,
  "name": "Live Cockpit",
  "theme": "mdash",
  "mapLive": true,
  "_about": "After the Live Cockpit Professional's standard view, generated by tools/gen_livecockpit.py (edit that and regenerate). One lcp effect layer draws the black backdrop, both scales (the right one mirrored: speed 0..200 mph / 0..330 km/h, revs 0..8000), the dark panels, the orange-red needles with BMW's red glow and a warm trail, the red rev band, the fuel dial (left) and the hybrid battery dial (right), the coolant and oil (left) and gearbox oil and fuel consumption (right) bracket gauges with the drive's average consumption, the lines and BMW's check-control tray; the numbers are text widgets. The oval map window opens while the Waze map shows, without a rebuild (mapLive). BMW's gear letter in the bottom strip stays uncovered. Widget reference: shared/hud.js header.",
